# GMS leaves a wall of fire standing for a few seconds, striking on its own
# clock. Nothing here lives on the ground, so it is what the WHOLE wall is
# worth: a Final Attack behind the fire spell that lit it, at GMS's own
# (10+4x)% chance of (30+x)% a hit.
#
# Twelve hits, not three. The client's three are one burst of the wall, which
# fires every 1.5 seconds (`subTime`) for the 4+floor(x/4) it stands -- four
# bursts once the duration passes five seconds, three below it. Folding the
# wall into the roll is what charges it to the swing that lit it.
#
# follows_skill_tag is what keeps it off Poison Breath, which is the whole
# point of the skill.
name: "Ignite"
skill_order: 6
description:
  "Grants Fire magic a chance to create a wall of fire at the target "
  "location."
kind: SKILL_KIND_PASSIVE
job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_FIRE_POISON_WIZARD
max_level: 10
follows_skill_tag: SKILL_TAG_FIRE
base {
  final_attack_chance: 0.14
  final_attack_pct: 0.31
  final_attack_lines: 12
}
per_level {
  final_attack_chance: 0.04
  final_attack_pct: 0.01
}
